ns/plugin-creator/agents/focused-reviewer.md` \u2014 live agent instruction that tells workers corroboration requires the same group id, directly encoding the semantics of the bug\\n- Main risk themes:\\n  - compatibility (Merged.group interface change breaks scorer.py)\\n  - verification (no test covers the new cross_group behavior)\\n  - documentation (orchestrator-playbook.md encodes the bug as correct pseudocode)\\n  - agent-instruction (focused-reviewer.md teaches agents the pre-fix corroboration model)\\n- Scope expansion:\\n  - `examples/solid-review-ab/runner/scorer.py` is a hard consumer not mentioned in the item description; it accesses `Merged.group` in 3 locations and will break at runtime if the field is removed; the A/B experiment harness (`scorer.py`, `cli.py`, `test_scorer*.py`) is a substantial additional scope that must be updated or verified compatible before the fix PR can land\\n\\n### Root-Cause Analysis\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-07-06T05:16:32.193798Z</sub>\\n\\n**Method**: 5-whys via evidence chain analysis\\n\\n**Evidence chain**:\\n1. Observed failure: cross_group corroboration signal is always False or absent in production\\n2. Why: The Merged dataclass has no cross_group field or property to track multi-group corroboration\\n3. Why: Findings from different rule groups on the same file location never merge into a single Merged entry\\n4. Why: The dedup key in reduce_findings() is (group, normalized_location), not just (location); different groups produce different keys\\n5. Why: The key design treats group as a dedup dimension, conflating dedup scope (per-group isolation) with corroboration scope (cross-group aggregation)\\n\\n**Root cause**: The deduplication key on line 149 includes `finding.group` as a component, which prevents findings from different rule groups on the same location from merging into a single Merged entry. This architectural decision makes cross-group corroboration impossible.\\n\\n**Fix locus**: Lines 149 (dedup key) and 66\u201379 (Merged dataclass) require restructuring:\\n- Change line 149 from `key = (finding.group, location)` to `key = location`\\n- Add `groups: set[str]` field to Merged dataclass (default factory: set)\\n- Add line tracking each group: `entry.groups.add(finding.group)`\\n- Add `cross_group` property returning `len(self.groups) >= 2`\\n</div>\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ensemble-rule-review/scripts/reduce.py` | Role: producer | Connection: the primary file containing the bug \u2014 `reduce_findings` dedup key and `Merged` dataclass | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ensemble-rule-review/scripts/test_reduce.py` | Role: test | Connection: direct `import reduce as r`; covers existing behavior but missing cross-group and `cross_group` property tests | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH | pattern: 'cross_group'\\n- `examples/solid-review-ab/runner/scorer.py` | Role: consumer | Connection: imports `reduce.py` via importlib; accesses `m.group`, `m.location`, `m.weight` on `Merged` objects in 3 sites | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: HIGH | pattern: 'm\\\\.group'\\n- `examples/solid-review-ab/tests/test_scorer.py` | Role: test | Connection: tests scorer which calls `reduce_findings`; fails if `Merged.group` removed without scorer update | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `examples/solid-review-ab/tests/test_scorer_independent.py` | Role: test | Connection: tests `score_arm_b` end-to-end; transitively depends on `Merged` interface via scorer | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ensemble-rule-review/references/orchestrator-playbook.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: contains literal pseudocode encoding the buggy `(group, location)` key | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH | pattern: 'key = \\\\(f\\\\[\\\"group\\\"\\\\]'\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ensemble-rule-review/SKILL.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: describes reducer keying on `(group, location)`; omits `cross_group` signal entirely | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM | pattern: '\\\\(group, location\\\\)'\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/agents/focused-reviewer.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: instructs workers that reducer requires same group id for corroboration \u2014 directly contradicts the fix intent | Action: AGENT_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH | pattern: 'keys on.*group.*location'\\n- `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml` | Role: ci | Connection: runs pytest (discovers test_reduce.py and examples/tests/) and ty/basedpyright type checking over all affected files | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ensemble-rule-review/scripts/conftest.py` | Role: configuration | Connection: pytest path setup; no API dependency | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `examples/solid-review-ab/runner/cli.py` | Role: consumer | Connection: indirect via scorer import; no direct `Merged` attribute access | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ensemble-rule-review/scripts/plan_ensemble.py` | Role: other-reference | Connection: co-located; mentioned together with reduce.py in docs but no code dependency | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n\\n### Tests\\n\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ensemble-rule-review/scripts/test_reduce.py` \u2014 imports `reduce as r`; tests `parse_report`, `reduce_findings`, `normalize_location`, `load_reports`, `main`; the existing test `test_corroboration_keys_on_group_not_rule` uses two workers in the **same group** (group 2) with different rule slugs \u2014 this test will continue to pass after the key change (same location still deduplicates); NO test covers cross-group corroboration (two different groups, same location \u2192 single merged entry with `cross_group=True`); NO test asserts the `cross_group` property | Risk: HIGH | Why: the entire purpose of this fix \u2014 enabling `cross_group` signal \u2014 has zero test coverage; fixing t